Replace the m-weigand-lineage EBC driver with hrdl's direct-mode rework.

PROVENANCE.  Generated 2026-08-25 from https://git.sr.ht/~hrdl/linux
branch v6.19_ebc_custom at 819ba1724a6f9147590a6e0eeaada28e2850464a --
the same commit doc/hrdl-evaluation.md pins, verified unmoved.  GPL-2.0,
as the kernel is.  Taken as a diff FROM our patched tree TO the same tree
with his EBC files substituted, so it applies after our seven and
replaces only the display driver.

WHAT IT SWAPS.  His rockchip_ebc.c (2527 lines) for ours (3481), his
drm_epd_helper.c, and the uapi header; adds rockchip_ebc.h and the
NEON blitter (rockchip_ebc_blit_neon.{c,h}, its own module); takes his
Kconfig additions including CONFIG_DRM_ROCKCHIP_EBC_3WIN_MODE.

The rockchip/Makefile hunk is hand-merged, not his verbatim: our
forward-port patch already adds rockchip_ebc.o there, so his context
did not match.  The merge keeps our line and adds his NEON object plus
its flags -- the blitter needs -mgeneral-regs-only REMOVED and
CC_FLAGS_FPU added, because kernel code is otherwise built with no FP
registers.

WHAT IS VERIFIED.  Against linux-7.1.8 with our pinenote_defconfig and
our other seven patches: Image, modules and both PineNote DTBs build,
EXIT=0, zero errors, one unused-variable warning.  Three modules link --
drm_epd_helper.ko (40,368 B), rockchip_ebc.ko (217,152 B) and
rockchip_ebc_blit_neon.ko (88,184 B) -- and modpost resolves the
cross-module symbols, which is what his EXPORT_SYMBOL(pvi_wbf_get_mode_index)
exists for.  CONFIG_DRM_ROCKCHIP_EBC_3WIN_MODE lands OFF under
olddefconfig, which is necessary: that config does not compile in his
tree (upstream-register item 15).

WHAT IS NOT.  Nothing has run.  The module is not loaded, does not probe,
does not bind, and no panel has shown a frame.  It also needs
custom_wf.bin at probe or it fails -EINVAL, and it needs an EBC device
node -- his branch carries NO dts at all, so the third clock direct mode
wants (cpll_333m) is on a branch we have not identified.  This patch is
NOT in %linux-pinenote-patches and reaches no shipping image; it exists
so linux-pinenote-hrdl-direct can be built and studied.

See doc/direct-mode-adoption.md.

